  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract activity in Missouri reached $11.4B in obligations for FY2026 to date. The state recorded 111,127 awards during the period, with an average award size of $103K. Obligations fell 18.2% year over year. The Department of Defense led buying in the state by obligating $8B, and the Department of Energy obligated $2.2B. THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest single contractor in Missouri with $5.3B in obligations. HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC obligated $2.2B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $3.5B, and Facilities Support Services follows with $2.3B. FY21 obligations were $13.3B, FY22 obligations were $11.2B, FY23 obligations were $15.6B, FY24 obligations were $16.2B, and FY25 obligations were $14B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the FY2026-to-date total of $11.4B?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounted for a large share by obligating $8B. Aircraft Manufacturing recorded $3.5B in obligations and Facilities Support Services recorded $2.3B. THE BOEING COMPANY and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC were major contractors, with $5.3B and $2.2B in obligations respectively. Obligations fell 18.2% compared with the prior year, reflecting lower fiscal-year-to-date spending."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where should vendors focus to win contracts in Missouri now?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing and aerospace supply chains show the largest obligations, led by Aircraft Manufacturing at $3.5B and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $721M. Facilities Support Services and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing also show scale, at $2.3B and $1.3B respectively. The Department of Defense and the Department of Energy are the largest buyers, obligating $8B and $2.2B respectively, and merit attention for business development."
      }
    ]
  },
